# SQL LOCK — always save SQL in the project

## Non-negotiable

1. **Any SQL you write or change MUST be saved in the repo** under `supabase/` (schema / migrations). Never leave SQL only in chat, comments, or ephemeral scratch.
2. **Every DB change** (tables, columns, indexes, RLS, functions, triggers — even tiny ones) updates project files so the schema stays the **current source of truth**.
3. Prefer:
   - `supabase/schema.sql` — full current schema (always keep it accurate)
   - `supabase/migrations/` — dated incremental files when changing an already-applied DB (`YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_short_name.sql`)
4. If you alter the DB via API logic assumptions, **update the SQL files in the same turn**.
5. Do **not** tell the user “run this SQL” without also writing that SQL into the project.

## Checklist before finishing any DB-related work

- [ ] SQL is on disk under `supabase/`
- [ ] `schema.sql` matches the intended live DB
- [ ] Small tweaks are not skipped — they are committed to files too
